rez!! And their finding was ?", "role": "confirmation", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:51:59Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "UC Berkeley", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:52:15Z", "username": "Dhruva", "text": "Was it x ray crystallography?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:52:18Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Asteroid hit created a winter and killed dinosaurs?", "role": "attempt", "is_correct": true, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:52:34Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Because of the dust and debris", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:54:21Z", "username": "Dhruva", "text": "Carbon dating?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:55:12Z", "username": "Dhruv", "text": "Not quite but, well I'll give it to you dude, you were the closest.. their finding was a theory called the Alvarez Hypothesis which states asteroids killed the dinosaurs, their main finding was the kpg line (cretaceous -palogene).. it states that in every natural sedimentary rock deposit around the world below which there are a world of fossils but above which there is nothing.. its usually marked by a single line of black, which Luis identified to be Iridium", "role": "answer_reveal", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:55:22Z", "username": "Dhruv", "text": ".", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17:56:27Z", "username": "Dhruv", "text": "For further reading: https://www2.lbl.gov/Science-Articles/Archive/luis-alvarez-iridium.html", "role": "confirmation", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2025-10-12T17